
Glossary:
OpenMS - Name of the project and our C++ library
OpenMS-TOPP-GUI - this repository: the Qt GUI layer of OpenMS (OpenMS_GUI library and the GUI tools)
TOPP - "The OpenMS PiPeline", a collection of chainable tools for flexible HPLC/MS workflows
TOPPAS - "The OpenMS PiPeline Assistant", a graphical tool to interactively build and run HPLC/MS workflows
TOPPView - Versatile viewer for HPLC/MS data
INI file - parameter configuration file, holding custom parameter settings for TOPP tools
INIFileEditor - graphical parameter editor for INI files
PR - Pull Request (on GitHub), i.e. integration of a new feature or bugfix
#<number>, e.g. #12 - a reference to an issue or pull request of this repository on GitHub, visit e.g.
  https://github.com/OpenMS/OpenMS-TOPP-GUI/pull/XXXX (replace XXXX with number of interest) for details;
  OpenMS/OpenMS#<number> refers to the OpenMS repository

Each release of OpenMS-TOPP-GUI is built against, and requires, the OpenMS release of the same version.
Changes of the GUI tools before 3.7.0 are listed in the CHANGELOG of OpenMS (https://github.com/OpenMS/OpenMS).



------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
----                         OpenMS-TOPP-GUI 3.7.0     (under development)            ----
----                         requires OpenMS 3.7.0                                    ----
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Build System:
  - BREAKING: The GUI layer of OpenMS (the OpenMS_GUI library, TOPPView, TOPPAS, INIFileEditor and the TOPP
    tools that need Qt, ExecutePipeline and ImageCreator) moved from the OpenMS repository into this repository,
    with the history of its files. It is built against an installed OpenMS of the same version (the OpenMS SDK
    or an installation built from source without the former WITH_GUI option); OpenMS itself no longer depends
    on Qt.
  - The GUI layer is installed into the OpenMS installation: its CMake package OpenMSGUI (target
    OpenMS::OpenMS_GUI) is also found through find_package(OpenMS COMPONENTS GUI), and its tool registry
    share/OpenMS/TOOLS/OpenMS-GUI.tsv adds ExecutePipeline and ImageCreator to the TOPP tools of OpenMS.
  - Installers of their own, as add-ons to the OpenMS installers of the same version:
    OpenMS-GUI-<version>-Win64.exe, OpenMS-GUI-<version>-macOS-<Silicon|Intel>.pkg and the Linux packages
    openms-gui (.deb, .rpm), which depend on the openms package.

Documentation:
  - The documentation of the GUI tools, the TOPPAS tutorial and the class documentation of the GUI library are
    built here (target 'doc') and installed into share/doc/html-gui; online at
    https://archive.openms.de/openms/Documentation/<release/version|nightly/latest>/html-gui/.
    The F1 help of TOPPView and TOPPAS opens it.
